<title>SINGAPORE: Hong Fok bounces back to 1st-half profit.</title>
<headline>Hong Fok bounces back to 1st-half profit.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    9.12   vs   5.99 (loss)</p>
<p>    Earnings per share (EPS) (cts)  6.69   vs   4.39 (loss)</p>
<p>    EPS fully diluted (cts)	   6.18   vs    NA</p>
<p>    Turnover			     38.04   vs  54.56</p>
<p>    Interest income		     0.16   vs   0.58</p>
<p>    Interest expense		   11.59   vs  16.62</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortization	 0.58   vs   1.22</p>
<p>    Income from associates	    0.84   vs    nil</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		     10.31   vs   7.19 (loss)</p>
<p>    Tax				     2.04   vs   1.06</p>
<p>    Minority interest		    nil   vs   2.25</p>
<p>Note - Hong Fok Ltd is a diversified property-based firm.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
